tools/asm-conformance/out_*.txt

# Covering-array corpora are oracle output. A local run happens in an emulated container, and the
# bit-identity contract only accepts goldens produced on real x86-64 CI, so a local copy must not
# be committed. The two below are the exception: they were produced by CI and are re-derived on
# every run, which is what makes the measured argument coverage checkable.
#
# The rule is a file glob rather than `tools/coverage/corpus/`: git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so a per-file negation under one has no effect.
tools/coverage/corpus/*
# {{BEGIN coverage corpora}}
